CVE-2026-44115 does not hide expansion tokens in environment-variable names: an allowlisted command containing an unquoted heredoc can hide shell expansion in the heredoc body, so the shell runs more than the approved text shows ([OpenClaw GHSA-x3h8-jrgh-p8jx, 2026-04-23](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/security/advisories/GHSA-x3h8-jrgh-p8jx)). Cyera reports about 65,000 instances on Shodan and about 180,000 on Zoomeye as two separate counts, not a combined 245,000, and its chain runs from a foothold inside the sandbox through the read escape and the heredoc flaw (credentials and files), then the loopback flaw (owner control), to the write escape (backdoors and persistence) ([Cyera, 2026-05-15](https://www.cyera.com/blog/claw-chain-cyera-research-unveil-four-chainable-vulnerabilities-in-openclaw)). The fix for all four is openclaw release 2026.4.22, the first release after 2026.4.21 ([OpenClaw GHSA-r6xh-pqhr-v4xh, 2026-04-23](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/security/advisories/GHSA-r6xh-pqhr-v4xh)). The 9.6 for CVE-2026-44112 is Cyera's CVSS 3.1 score; VulnCheck scores it 8.4 in CVSS 4.0 ([VulnCheck, CVE-2026-44112](https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/openclaw-symlink-swap-race-condition-in-openshell-fs-bridge-writes)), and OpenClaw rates CVE-2026-44115 moderate ([OpenClaw GHSA-x3h8-jrgh-p8jx, 2026-04-23](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/security/advisories/GHSA-x3h8-jrgh-p8jx)).
